   "textLength": 760,
   "text": "Most manufacturers recommend turntable stylus replacement at around 1,000 hours of record playing time. So if you’re using your turntable for an hour or so per day on average, ideally you should be changing the stylus every couple of years. This varies depending on the manufacturer and what type of materials they’re using.\nIt’s worth checking the manufacturer’s recommended lifespan for your stylus",
